;; BigNat's arithmetic in Go (queue 430): ghc-internal's bignum backend is the native one (HES7 (a)), Haskell loops over
;; WordArray#s that hsi interprets word by word, quadratic in the operands' size for a product, a quotient or a gcd (T22671's
;; show of 2^(2^20): 0.05 s on GHC's GMP, past the check's 60 s on hsi). The pure functions of GHC.Internal.Bignum.BigNat
;; below (BigNat# -> BigNat# -> ...: a trimmed WordArray#, no trailing zero word, zero the empty array) are computed by
;; math/big instead when both operands are BigNats and the case is an ordinary one; any other case (a zero divisor, an
;; unsafe subtraction's misuse) runs the closure's own code, so every exception and edge stays GHC's. The result is the
;; same number, trimmed as the Haskell code trims it.


